@startuml
title PlugIt - Portable Micro-Service Integration Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "External User / System" as ExternalUser
actor "Service Developer" as Developer
actor "Operator / Administrator" as Operator

package "PlugIt Proxy (Host Platform)" {
  component "Shared User Experience" as SharedUX
  component "PlugIt Proxy API Endpoint" as ProxyAPI
  component "Standalone Proxy Mail Workflow" as MailWorkflow
  database "Proxy Data Store" as ProxyDataStore
}

package "PlugIt Service (mutually isolated, 1..n)" {
  component "Service Application" as ServiceApp
  component "PlugIt API Client" as ApiClient
  component "Service Configuration\n<project + local/private settings>" as ServiceConfig
  component "Schema Upgrade Files\n(version-managed migrations)" as Migrations
  database "Service Data Store" as ServiceDataStore
}

database "Database Technology\n<MySQL / SQLite>" as DBTech
queue "Mailbox / Inbound Email" as Mailbox

ExternalUser --> SharedUX : accesses services
SharedUX ..> ProxyAPI
ProxyAPI --> ProxyDataStore : reads/writes

ExternalUser --> ProxyAPI : external-to-proxy access
ProxyAPI --> ServiceApp : PlugIt protocol
ProxyAPI ..> ApiClient : programmatic API

ServiceApp --> ServiceConfig : reads API_URL, SQLALCHEMY_URL,\nDEBUG, PI_BASE_URL, PI_ALLOWED_NETWORKS
ServiceConfig ..> ApiClient : provides main endpoint URL
ServiceApp --> ApiClient : uses capabilities\n(users, tags, orgs, members, email, forum)
ApiClient --> ProxyAPI : API requests to main endpoint

ServiceApp --> ServiceDataStore : configured connection
Migrations --> ServiceDataStore : applies schema upgrades
ServiceDataStore --> DBTech

Mailbox --> MailWorkflow : inbound email
MailWorkflow --> MailWorkflow : validate routing token\ncheck auto-response\nsuppress / extract text
MailWorkflow --> ServiceApp : invoke mail handler\n(decoded routing + payload)

Developer --> ServiceConfig : defines settings and models
Developer --> Migrations : generates upgrade files
Operator --> ServiceConfig : maintains private local settings\n(excluded from source control)
Operator --> DBTech : provisions and configures

note right of MailWorkflow
  Example / standalone proxy scope only.
  Validates hash:data routing tokens using
  SHA-512 digest slice [30:42] and mail secret;
  drops auto-response messages; removes
  successfully processed messages.
end note

note bottom of ServiceConfig
  Private deployment settings live in local
  configuration excluded from source control.
end note

@enduml
